      "side": 1,
      "message": "Whatever the preferred way is, I\u0027d love to give it a try in the next days, if that could be a help. Let\u0027s see if I got the idea.\n\nWe would hardcode the default in LineageParts, expose it in some getter function, that is then used also from LineageBatteryLights as a default in the call to getIntForUser. This way we avoid duplication of the default value. That would likely also apply to the two other def_ bools in BatteryLightSettings.\n\nI might be wrong, but it seems that in contrast to the bools the default light colors are fetched from com.android.internal.R.integer.config_notificationsBattery...ARGB both in BatteryLightSettings and in LineageBatteryLights – so no duplication. The default brightness is hardcoded twice: in BatteryBrightnessPreference and in LineageBatteryLights.\n\nWould it make sense to align the handling of the various defaults?",
      "revId": "bbaa0be775821d0d649cf6dafa3c3ec6bc36ed7d",
